# Ground truth for squat_10_fast.csv
#
# 10 squats at a deliberately quick pace, front pocket, Pixel, ~99 Hz.
#
# This is the trace that exposed the cooldown conflation. With the original
# cooldownMs = 2000 the detector found 5 of these 10 reps: at a ~1.9 s cadence most reps
# begin less than 2 s after the previous one ended, and were discarded as rebound. The
# reps are plainly in the signal and clear every other guard.
#
# It also showed that no single cooldown value could work. This set needs 900 ms or less;
# squat_10_hit needs 1000 ms or more to keep a 0.60-amplitude wobble out. Those
# requirements do not overlap, so the fix was to split the cooldown's two jobs -- rebound
# suppression stays with cooldownMs, wobble rejection moved to minAmplitude and
# minRepDurationMs -- rather than to search harder for a number.

exercise = SQUAT

# Set boundaries read from the signal, not estimated. The 10 squats run 8628 -> 27376 ms
# at a 1.7-2.2 s start-to-start cadence. Before them: handling bursts ending at 3822 ms,
# leaving a 4.8 s gap. After them: a settling burst starting at 27789 ms, leaving only a
# 413 ms gap -- hence the unrounded upper bound. The count is insensitive to both bounds;
# anything from 4000-27700 inwards yields the same 10 reps.
reps = 10
setStartMs = 6000
setEndMs = 27500
tolerance = 0

# 10 reps plus two handling artifacts: the phone going into the pocket at ~1.9 s and
# coming back out at ~30.5 s. Both are large movements that no guard rejects, and neither
# is meant to be rejected -- excluding them is a session-trimming job.
fullTraceEvents = 12

# No still period was recorded on this trace, so it declares no quiet window.

notes = participant: Mohit (fast pace, ~1.9s per rep). Pixel, ~99Hz, front pocket. The trace that exposed the cooldown conflation.
